# JUCE UTF-8 string literals

`juce::String(const char*)` only accepts ASCII. Multi-byte UTF-8 in a narrow
literal (ellipsis `…`, em dash `—`, arrows `→`, `©`, `∞`, smart quotes, etc.)
becomes mojibake.

## Required

- Include `Utf8.h` and wrap every non-ASCII narrow string literal with `utf8("…")`.
- Prefer readable UTF-8 characters in the literal; the helper is `utf8()` in
  `native/plugin_host_app/Source/Utf8.h`.
- When editing UI copy, tooltips, alerts, status text, or error strings, audit
  nearby literals in the same change — do not leave other unwrapped non-ASCII
  strings in that file.

```cpp
// BAD
setStatus("No plugins — use More plugins…");

// GOOD
#include "Utf8.h"
setStatus(utf8("No plugins — use More plugins…"));
```

ASCII-only literals may stay as plain `"..."`. Comments do not need `utf8()`.
